<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Is it DHA-compliant to sell prepaid treatment packages?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes — selling a defined number of sessions at a bulk rate is a standard commercial arrangement. Price, session count, and terms are fine to discuss; any implied guarantee of outcome is not, and should only come from a practitioner within a consultation."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How is a clinic membership different from a package?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A package is a defined, prepaid number of sessions for a specific treatment. A membership is typically a recurring monthly fee covering administrative visits or a discount rate across treatments, without a fixed prepaid session count."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What happens if a patient doesn't use all their prepaid sessions?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"This should be decided before launch — most UAE clinics set an expiry window and a clear refund or extension policy for unused sessions, applied consistently to every patient."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can package pricing be advertised, or does it need special handling?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Package pricing can be promoted like any commercial offer, as long as the language stays focused on bulk pricing and scheduling convenience rather than implying guaranteed results."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Should a new clinic start with packages right away?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Usually not immediately — packages work best once a clinic already has patients returning predictably for a specific treatment."}}]}</script>

			
			
